# Expression kind

With `kind: Expression` the code block is a single C# expression. RunPad evaluates it and
renders the result as if you had called `.Dump()` on it. There is no trailing semicolon.

```csharp run
Enumerable.Range(1, 10)
    .Where(n => n % 2 == 0)
    .Select(n => new { Number = n, Square = n * n, IsLarge = n * n > 25 })
```
